# Normalise line endings in the repository and check out LF everywhere.
#
# There are two working copies of this project: the canonical one under WSL (where the build runs,
# requiring JDK 25 + Maven from ~/.local/tools/env.sh) and a mirrored one under
# C:\Users\thevi\projects on the Windows side. Without this file, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf enabled rewrites every line of every text file, and the two trees report each other's
# files as modified forever — a permanent, meaningless diff that hides real changes.
#
# eol=lf keeps the working copies byte-identical; the files are plain YAML, Java and Markdown, none of
# which require CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Build output and IDE state are never tracked.
target/ binary
*.jar binary
*.class binary
